{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-75569","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108683","text":"Skill 01 — The Ten Protocols"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75571","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108684","text":"OS-001 through OS-010: what each protocol specifies, which product implements it, and the cognitive science behind it. Eight cognitive primitives plus two cross-cutting protocols (PRISM diagnostic, PULSE temporal)."}]}],"id":"blk-75570","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-75572","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108685","text":"Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-75573","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108686","text":"OpenSentience publishes ten numbered protocols organized in two layers:"}]},{"id":"blk-75574","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75576","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108687","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive primitives (OS-001 — OS-008)"},{"id":"spn-108688","text":" — eight individual capabilities,"}]}],"id":"blk-75575","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75577","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108689","text":"each grounded in a cognitive science thread."}]},{"id":"blk-75578","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75580","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108690","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cross-cutting protocols (OS-009 PRISM, OS-010 PULSE)"},{"id":"spn-108691","text":" — two sibling"}]}],"id":"blk-75579","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75581","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108692","text":"protocols that sit above the cognitive primitives and above the [&] structural composition layer. PULSE declares how every loop in the ecosystem cycles, nests, and signals; PRISM measures how well those loops actually learn over time."}]},{"id":"blk-75582","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108693","text":"The protocols are independent specifications — they can be adopted individually or composed together. A system may publish a PULSE manifest without implementing any cognitive primitive, and PRISM can benchmark any PULSE-conforming system without bespoke per-system integration."}]},{"id":"blk-75583","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108694","text":"OS-001: Continual Learning"}]},{"id":"blk-75584","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108695","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-108696","text":" Hippocampal consolidation (McClelland et al. 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-75585","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108697","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-75586","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75588","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108698","text":"Three node types: episodic (events), semantic (facts), procedural (workflows)"}]}],"id":"blk-75587","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75590","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108699","text":"Typed, weighted edges between nodes"}]}],"id":"blk-75589","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75592","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108700","text":"Confidence scores with evidence-calibrated assignment"}]}],"id":"blk-75591","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75594","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108701","text":"Consolidation cycle: decay low-confidence nodes, prune stale entries,"}]}],"id":"blk-75593","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75595","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108702","text":"merge near-duplicates, strengthen co-retrieved edges"}]},{"id":"blk-75596","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75598","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108703","text":"Memory timescales: working memory (session), short-term (hours), long-term"}]}],"id":"blk-75597","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75599","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108704","text":"(persistent)"}]},{"id":"blk-75600","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108705","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-108706","text":" New memories must be stored quickly (hippocampal fast-write) without disrupting existing knowledge (neocortical slow-consolidation). This maps to immediate ETS/SQLite writes with background consolidation."}]},{"id":"blk-75601","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108707","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-108708","text":" Graphonomous ("},{"id":"spn-108709","marks":["code"],"text":"store_node"},{"id":"spn-108710","text":", "},{"id":"spn-108711","marks":["code"],"text":"store_edge"},{"id":"spn-108712","text":", "},{"id":"spn-108713","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-108714","text":", "},{"id":"spn-108715","marks":["code"],"text":"run_consolidation"},{"id":"spn-108716","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-75602","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108717","text":"OS-002: Topological Routing (kappa)"}]},{"id":"blk-75603","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108718","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-108719","text":" Working memory gating (O'Reilly & Frank 2006)"}]},{"id":"blk-75604","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108720","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-75605","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75607","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108721","text":"The kappa parameter: a measure of cyclicity in a knowledge subgraph"}]}],"id":"blk-75606","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75609","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108722","text":"Strongly connected component (SCC) detection on retrieved neighborhoods"}]}],"id":"blk-75608","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75611","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108723","text":"Routing decision: kappa = 0 implies fast path (acyclic, no conflict),"}]}],"id":"blk-75610","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75612","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108724","text":"kappa > 0 implies deliberate path (cycles exist, may contain contradictions)"}]},{"id":"blk-75613","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75615","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108725","text":"Topological features: SCC count, max SCC size, edge density within cycles"}]}],"id":"blk-75614","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75616","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108726","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-108727","text":" The prefrontal cortex gates information into working memory based on relevance and conflict signals. Kappa serves as the conflict signal — cyclic knowledge regions indicate unresolved tension that requires deliberation before action."}]},{"id":"blk-75617","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108728","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-108729","text":" Graphonomous routing layer ("},{"id":"spn-108730","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_analyze"},{"id":"spn-108731","text":", "},{"id":"spn-108732","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-108733","text":" topology annotations)"}]},{"id":"blk-75618","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108734","text":"OS-003: Deliberation Orchestrator"}]},{"id":"blk-75619","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108735","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-108736","text":" Dual-process theory (Kahneman 2011)"}]},{"id":"blk-75620","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108737","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-75621","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75623","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108738","text":"Four-phase deliberation: bid, debate, vote, commit"}]}],"id":"blk-75622","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75625","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108739","text":"Argumentation framework: claims, warrants, rebuttals"}]}],"id":"blk-75624","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75627","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108740","text":"Consensus mechanisms: majority, supermajority, unanimity"}]}],"id":"blk-75626","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75629","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108741","text":"Timeout and escalation policies"}]}],"id":"blk-75628","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75631","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108742","text":"Triggered when kappa routing indicates deliberation is needed"}]}],"id":"blk-75630","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75632","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108743","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-108744","text":" System 1 (fast, automatic) handles routine decisions. System 2 (slow, deliberate) engages when conflict is detected. The kappa threshold is the trigger that shifts from fast to deliberate processing."}]},{"id":"blk-75633","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108745","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-108746","text":" AgenTroMatic ("},{"id":"spn-108747","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"},{"id":"spn-108748","text":" tool in Graphonomous provides the single-agent deliberation path)"}]},{"id":"blk-75634","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108749","text":"OS-004: Attention Engine"}]},{"id":"blk-75635","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108750","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-108751","text":" Endogenous attention (Desimone & Duncan 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-75636","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108752","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-75637","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75639","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108753","text":"Three-phase cycle: survey (scan environment), triage (rank by salience),"}]}],"id":"blk-75638","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75640","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108754","text":"dispatch (act on highest-priority items)"}]},{"id":"blk-75641","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75643","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108755","text":"Salience scoring: combines urgency, recency, goal relevance, and confidence"}]}],"id":"blk-75642","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75645","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108756","text":"Goal bias: active goals increase salience of related knowledge"}]}],"id":"blk-75644","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75647","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108757","text":"Dispatch modes: act (execute), learn (gather more context), escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-75646","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75648","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108758","text":"(request human intervention), idle (nothing needed)"}]},{"id":"blk-75649","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108759","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-108760","text":" Biological attention is goal-directed (endogenous) not just stimulus-driven (exogenous). The attention engine prioritizes based on the agent's active goals, not just what is new or loud."}]},{"id":"blk-75650","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108761","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-108762","text":" Graphonomous attention module ("},{"id":"spn-108763","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"},{"id":"spn-108764","text":", "},{"id":"spn-108765","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_run_cycle"},{"id":"spn-108766","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-75651","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108767","text":"OS-005: Model Tier Adaptation"}]},{"id":"blk-75652","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108768","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-108769","text":" Resource rationality (Lieder & Griffiths 2020)"}]},{"id":"blk-75653","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108770","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-75654","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75656","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108771","text":"Three tiers: "},{"id":"spn-108772","marks":["code"],"text":"local_small"},{"id":"spn-108773","text":" (8B parameter models), "},{"id":"spn-108774","marks":["code"],"text":"local_large"},{"id":"spn-108775","text":" (70B+),"}]}],"id":"blk-75655","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75657","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108776","marks":["code"],"text":"cloud_frontier"},{"id":"spn-108777","text":" (largest available)"}]},{"id":"blk-75658","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75660","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108778","text":"Same topology and tool surface at every tier — only depth and latency differ"}]}],"id":"blk-75659","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75662","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108779","text":"Escalation rules: when local_small confidence is below threshold, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-75661","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75663","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108780","text":"to local_large; when local_large is insufficient, escalate to cloud_frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-75664","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75666","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108781","text":"Budget constraints: token limits, latency targets, cost caps per tier"}]}],"id":"blk-75665","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75667","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108782","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-108783","text":" Optimal cognition allocates computational resources proportional to decision importance. Simple decisions use fast/cheap processing; high-stakes decisions justify expensive computation."}]},{"id":"blk-75668","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108784","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-108785","text":" Graphonomous and Agentelic (tier selection and escalation logic)"}]},{"id":"blk-75669","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108786","text":"OS-006: Agent Governance Shim"}]},{"id":"blk-75670","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108787","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-108788","text":" Executive function (Miyake et al. 2000)"}]},{"id":"blk-75671","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108789","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-75672","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75674","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108790","text":"Permission taxonomy: filesystem, network, tool_invocation, graph_access"}]}],"id":"blk-75673","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75676","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108791","text":"Lifecycle state machine: installed, enabled, running, disabled, removed"}]}],"id":"blk-75675","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75678","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108792","text":"Graduated autonomy: observe, advise, act"}]}],"id":"blk-75677","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75680","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108793","text":"Append-only audit trail with typed events"}]}],"id":"blk-75679","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75682","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108794","text":"OTP-native implementation: GenStateMachine, ETS, DynamicSupervisor"}]}],"id":"blk-75681","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75683","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108795","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-108796","text":" Executive function provides inhibitory control (permissions), task switching (lifecycle), and cognitive flexibility (autonomy levels). Without executive function, an agent cannot self-regulate — it either does nothing or does everything."}]},{"id":"blk-75684","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108797","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-108798","text":" "},{"id":"spn-108799","marks":["code"],"text":"open_sentience"},{"id":"spn-108800","text":" hex package (this project)"}]},{"id":"blk-75685","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108801","text":"OS-007: Adversarial Robustness"}]},{"id":"blk-75686","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108802","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-108803","text":" Immune system — self/non-self discrimination"}]},{"id":"blk-75687","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108804","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-75688","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75690","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108805","text":"Five threat categories: prompt injection, model poisoning, side-channel,"}]}],"id":"blk-75689","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75691","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108806","text":"identity spoofing, resource exhaustion"}]},{"id":"blk-75692","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75694","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108807","text":"Detection rules per category"}]}],"id":"blk-75693","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75696","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108808","text":"Defense protocols: quarantine, circuit-break, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-75695","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75698","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108809","text":"Integration with OS-006 for permission revocation and OS-008 for circuit"}]}],"id":"blk-75697","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75699","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108810","text":"breaking"}]},{"id":"blk-75700","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108811","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-108812","text":" OpenSentience security module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-75701","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108813","text":"OS-008: Agent Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-75702","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108814","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-108815","text":" Supervisory attentional system (Norman & Shallice 1986)"}]},{"id":"blk-75703","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108816","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-75704","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75706","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108817","text":"Pipeline ordering enforcement (retrieve → route → act → learn)"}]}],"id":"blk-75705","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75708","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108818","text":"Quality gates between pipeline stages"}]}],"id":"blk-75707","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75710","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108819","text":"Sprint contracts: bounded execution with explicit goals and success criteria"}]}],"id":"blk-75709","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75712","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108820","text":"Context management: 60% threshold, compaction, Graphonomous overflow"}]}],"id":"blk-75711","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75714","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108821","text":"Generator-evaluator separation for adversarial grading"}]}],"id":"blk-75713","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75715","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108822","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-108823","text":" OpenSentience harness module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-75716","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-108824","text":"OS-009: PRISM — Protocol for Rating Iterative System Memory"}]},{"id":"blk-75717","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108825","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-108826","text":" Meta-cognition + psychometrics (Item Response Theory, signal detection theory)"}]},{"id":"blk-75718","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108827","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-75719","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75721","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108828","text":"9 continual-learning dimensions (retention, plasticity, transfer,"}]}],"id":"blk-75720","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-75722","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108829","text":"contradiction handling, etc.)"}]},{"id":"blk-75723","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-75725","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-108830","text":"4-phase evaluation loop: compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose"}]}],"id